===Etymology 3===
{{ja-see|荒れ}}

===Etymology 4===
{{ja-kanjitab|alt=吾,我}}
The long form of {{m|ja|あ|tr=a|t=[[I]], [[me]]}}. From {{suffix|ja|あ|tr1=a|れ|tr2=re|pos2=nominalizing suffix}}

Fell into disuse in roughly the [[w:Heian period|Heian period]],<ref name="DJR">{{R:Daijirin}}</ref> when it was replaced by {{ja-r|われ}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{ja-pron|acc=h}} {{rfv-pron|ja}}<!--is this the modern pitch accent used when reading old texts aloud?-->

====Pronoun====
{{ja-pos|pronoun}}

# {{lb|ja|sort=あれ|obsolete}} ''[[first person|first-person]] [[personal pronoun]]'': [[I]], [[me]]
#* {{RQ:Genji Monogatari|54}}
#*: {{quote|ja|...と、聞こえ動かして、几帳のもとに、おし寄せたてまつりたれば、'''あれ'''にもあらず、居給へるけはい...}}

===Etymology 5===
{{etymid|ja|有れ}}
{{ja-kanjitab|alt=有れ,在れ}}

====Pronunciation====
{{ja-pron}}

====Verb====
{{ja-verb form|hhira=あれ}}

# {{lb|ja|classical|literary}} {{inflection of|ja|あり|tr=ari|t=to [[exist]]||imperative}}; {{lb|ja|modern language}} {{inflection of|ja|ある|tr=aru|t=to [[exist]]||imperative}}
#: {{ja-usex|[[光]]'''あれ'''|ひかり '''あれ'''|let there be light}}
#: {{ja-usex|[[乞う]][[期待|ご期%待]]'''あれ'''|こ.う ご-き%たい '''あれ'''|{{q|modern language|formal}} please stay tuned}}
#: {{ja-usex|[[試し|お試し]]'''あれ'''|お-ためし '''あれ'''|{{q|modern language|formal}} please try it out}}
#: {{ja-usex|[[ご覧]]'''あれ'''|ご-らん '''あれ'''|please look}}
#* {{quote-av|1=ja|year=1979|author=w:Yoshiyuki Tomino|actor=w:Katsuji Mori|role=w:Garma Zabi|title=w:Mobile Suit Gundam|season=|number=10|time=|text=}}
#*: {{ja-x|ジオン [[公%国]] [[に]] [[栄%光]] '''あれ'''！|ジオン こう%こく に えい%こう '''あれ'''！|Glory to the Principality of Zeon!}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Although it remains grammatically correct in modern language, there are few, if any, situations in which it is used, outside of stock formal phrases inherited from the classical language.

